{
  "content": {
    "items": [
      {
        "description": "entry_points as concrete file:symbol (never a phrase) · the topic closure definition · the depth (shallow/extract/deep) · the exclusion list · the utility filter. The Scope Block is echoed into the conversation BEFORE any pebble write.",
        "enforcement": "strict",
        "id": "6d4d722f-af22-4c75-b455-55cc7896b831",
        "status": "verified",
        "text": "Emit the SCOPE BLOCK before reading any code"
      },
      {
        "description": "If the topic resolves to more than one plausible entry symbol, list the candidates and confirm with the user. Extraction from the wrong entry is 100% wasted work.",
        "enforcement": "strict",
        "id": "d628f785-d0ac-460f-9cf7-a6b313b138dc",
        "status": "verified",
        "text": "Ambiguous entry point? Ask BEFORE extracting, never after"
      },
      {
        "description": "A node is in scope iff it is reachable FROM an entry point via the call/import graph (map-neighbors --out, map-callers to verify direction). Upstream callers of the entry point are OUT. Siblings are OUT. The processes that happen BEFORE the topic are OUT — always.",
        "enforcement": "strict",
        "id": "0cf0c4b0-79c7-4163-803b-264f7e796076",
        "status": "verified",
        "text": "The topic closure is FORWARD reachability only"
      },
      {
        "description": "A callee with codebase-wide fan-in ≥5 (from the map), or matching the utility list (log, validate, auth-check, serialize, config), appears only inside a step's description — never as its own node or workflow.",
        "enforcement": "strict",
        "id": "8315a3ae-48ed-42fb-923f-a93c6cac60f8",
        "status": "verified",
        "text": "Shared utilities are never nodes"
      },
      {
        "description": "A node citing a file the map doesn't place in the closure is rejected. No citation = no node.",
        "enforcement": "strict",
        "id": "38ca81e4-1ffe-4e5d-90fc-1479c742346c",
        "status": "verified",
        "text": "Every node cites a code location inside the declared closure"
      },
      {
        "description": "Reachable-but-excluded items are listed with reason codes (utility, out-of-topic, upstream). A non-trivial topic with zero exclusions means the boundary wasn't actually applied.",
        "enforcement": "strict",
        "id": "ad012b64-da86-46f7-b47f-1f18146127b6",
        "status": "verified",
        "text": "Emit the exclusion list — empty is a red flag"
      },
      {
        "description": "Count the branches in the source closure and the condition nodes emitted; unexplained deltas block completion.",
        "enforcement": "strict",
        "id": "17d4d150-872d-4afe-bce5-9aae62a26d2d",
        "status": "verified",
        "text": "Reconcile branches vs nodes before publishing"
      },
      {
        "description": "Needing a second start node means the scope should SPLIT into another workflow, not grow.",
        "enforcement": "strict",
        "id": "3a7424a9-0f78-49e0-b903-fd911e368ad2",
        "status": "verified",
        "text": "One workflow per entry point"
      }
    ],
    "kind": "checklist"
  },
  "createdAt": "2026-07-21T14:32:38.718Z",
  "description": "Off-topic extraction is the observed failure: extracting things unrelated to the requested topic. The boundary is mechanical, declared up front, and every emitted node must prove it belongs.",
  "id": "4baf83c3-426f-467b-8642-e79a9683cce0",
  "name": "Extraction — scope boundary (topic is law)",
  "refs": [
    {
      "id": "bb777dad-e3c3-40c7-9dd4-1f36e53c8ea2",
      "label": "The code map — a real dependency graph",
      "path": ".pebbles/knowledge/system/code-map.pebble",
      "pebbleId": "9f749a7c-f031-4956-9381-5f48bfe28ede",
      "section": "knowledge",
      "targetKind": "pebble"
    }
  ],
  "status": "verified",
  "tags": [
    "system"
  ],
  "type": "rule",
  "updatedAt": "2026-07-28T03:27:29.181Z",
  "version": 1
}
